==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|mawke}}, {{m|enm|moke}}, a contraction of {{m|enm|mathek}}, {{m|enm|maddok}}, from {{der|en|non|maðkr||maggot}}, a diminutive of a base from {{der|en|gem-pro|*maþô||worm}} (compare {{cog|ang|maþa}}), from {{der|en|ine-pro|*mat-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*mot-}} used in reference to insects and vermin. Cognate with {{cog|da|maddike}}, {{cog|sv|mask}}, archaic  {{cog|en|maddock}} (modern {{m|en|maggot}}).

